ence (blocked)\n4. Uncertain dependencies (review-required)\n5. Duplicate unit IDs (detected)\n6. No copy invented or reordered (provider is read-only)\n7. Answer-before-question ambiguity (detected)\n8. Pronoun antecedent edges validated\n9. Callback edges validated\n10. Step-order constraints validated\n11. Missing antecedent with evidence (forbidden)\n12. Missing unit (forbidden)\n13. Reviewer boolean ignored (graph validation wins)\n14. Repeat tutorial step detected15. Unsupported causality without evidence (review-required)\n\nLet me write both files now.\n\nFor the provider, I'll add the answer-before-question scan. Let me find the right place to insert it - after the edge loop but before the tutorial steps check.\n\nLet me re-read the full provider to find the exact insertion point...\n\nThe flow is:\n1. Edge loop (lines ~130-240ish)\n2. Tutorial steps scan3. Coverage gaps scan\n4. Base object construction\n\nI'll add the answer-before-question scan between the edge loop and the tutorial steps scan.\n\nNow let me write the code. I need to be very careful with the apply_patch format.\n\nLet me plan the exact patch for chronology.mjs. I need to add the answer-before-question ambiguity check. Let me find the exact line to insert after.\n\nLooking at the code flow:\n```js\n  // ... end of edge loop ...\n\n  const tutorialSteps = new Map();\n```\n\nI'll insert the answer-before-question check before the tutorial steps scan.\n\nLet me look at the exact content around the insertion point."}}
